# <%= className %> e2e tests

End-to-end tests with [Playwright](https://playwright.dev) — full user journeys
against a running stack. Headless by default (`use.headless: true`), Chromium only.

## Setup

```bash
cd <%= fileName %>
npm install
npx playwright install chromium
cp .env.example .env
```

## Running

```bash
nx e2e <%= fileName %>        # headless
npm run e2e:headed            # watch the browser
npm run e2e:ui                # Playwright UI mode
npm run report                # open the last HTML report
```

- `BASE_URL` — where the app is served (default `http://localhost:3000`)
- `WEB_SERVER_CMD` — if set, Playwright starts the stack itself and waits for
  `BASE_URL` before running (e.g. `nx run-many -t serve`). Unset = assume it's
  already up.

Nx does not cache the `e2e` target.
